<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.7: Admin Selects Training Modules for Creates Campai=
gn Setup (Step-7)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to select the training language, assignment type, an=
d training modules to be assigned to employees so that I can tailor the tra=
ining content for the phishing campaign and ensure it reaches the correct a=
udience.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>This use case outlines the process by which the Admin can select the tra=
ining language, assignment method, and specific training modules during the=
 campaign creation process. The Admin is able to filter, sort, and preview =
training modules before finalizing their selection. Additionally, the Admin=
 can specify the training scope, assign deadlines, and toggle advanced opti=
ons for customization. Once all selections are made, the Admin can proceed =
with the campaign setup.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Selects the language, assignment method, and tra=
ining modules for the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Validates the selected options, assigns trainin=
g modules, and ensures the modules are assigned according to the Admin's pr=
eferences.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin is logged into the Aspire Tech portal with necessary privilege=
s to create campaigns.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin is on the "Create Campaign" screen, where the "Training Module=
s" section is available.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system is operational and supports training module selection and ass=
ignment.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The selected training language, assignment method, and training modules =
are saved and linked to the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can proceed to the next steps of the campaign creation process=
 by clicking the "Save &amp; Continue" button.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Access Training Module Selection</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin accesses the Campaign Creation Dashboard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the <strong>Training Language</strong> dropdown list=
 (English, Spanish, Arabic, Bengali, Portuguese, French, Russian, Indonesia=
n, Hindi, Mandarin Chinese), where the Admin can select the language for th=
e training modules:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Default Language</strong>: English (preselected).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Other Languages</strong>: Additional languages available in the =
system.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 2: Select Assignment Method</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the assignment method from the dropdown:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Assign All</strong>: All selected training modules will be assig=
ned to users.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Intelligently Assign</strong>: One of the selected training modu=
les will be assigned to users based on data. Based on Phishing email templa=
te type (Credential Harvesting, Financial Fraud, Malware Distribution, Data=
 Theft, Account Takeover, Ransomware, Spyware, Business Email Compromise, P=
hishing for Information, CEO Fraud), training module will automatically ass=
ign.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 3: View Available Training Modules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The system displays the <strong>Training Module Selection</strong> secti=
on, where the Admin can choose from a list of available training modules.</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Filter</strong>: Filter modules by category, type, or difficulty=
.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Sort</strong>: Sort by popularity (most to least) or Alphabetica=
l.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Search</strong>: Search for specific training modules.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 4: Use the Filter Option (Optional)</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin can click on the <strong>Filter</strong> button to refine the =
selection of training modules.</p></li>
<li>
<p>A modal window opens with additional filtering options:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Training Language</strong>: Admin selects the language for the t=
raining.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Days Until Due</strong>: Admin sets the number of days before th=
e training is due.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Assignments</strong>: Admin selects the assignment method.</p></=
li>
<li>
<p><strong>Hide Advanced Options</strong>: Admin can toggle to show or hide=
 advanced options.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Training Scope</strong>: Admin specifies the scope of training (=
e.g., employees who clicked on phishing links or were compromised).</p></li=
>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 5: Select Training Modules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin selects one or more training modules to be assigned to employe=
es.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can preview the selected modules before finalizing the selecti=
on.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A preview of the training module is displayed, showing a brief overview =
of the content.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 6: Confirm Selection</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Once the training modules are selected, the Admin confirms the selection=
 and clicks <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> to proceed to the next ste=
p in the campaign creation process.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Input Field Validation Table</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"c0=
4acd9d-a608-4a5d-9043-3a09f085ee7b" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Field</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Validation Rules</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Training Language</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Admin must select a language from the dropdow=
n. <strong>Default</strong>: English.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Assignment Type</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Admin must select either "Assign All" or "Int=
elligently Assign".</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Training Modules</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Admin must select at least one training modul=
e.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Module Preview</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Optional</strong>: Admin can preview selected training modules b=
efore assignment.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Days Until Due</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Optional</strong>: Admin can set a due date for the training.</p=
></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Training Scope</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Admin must specify the scope of training (e.g=
., employees who clicked on payloads or were compromised).</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Exception / Alternative Scenarios</strong></p>
<p><strong>Scenario 1</strong>: <strong>No training module selected</strong=
></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>System Behavior</strong>: Display error message: "You must selec=
t at least one training module."</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Scenario 2</strong>: <strong>Invalid training module selection</=
strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>System Behavior</strong>: Display error message: "Invalid traini=
ng module. Please select a valid option."</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Scenario 3</strong>: <strong>No assignment method selected</stro=
ng></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>System Behavior</strong>: Display error message: "Please select =
a valid assignment method."</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Scenario 4</strong>: <strong>No training scope selected</strong>=
</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>System Behavior</strong>: Display error message: "Please specify=
 a valid training scope."</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"00=
02556f-978f-420b-9e69-3d5c2f2e870c" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-01</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select a language from the dropdown list.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can choose a language from the available list (default is English)=
.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-02</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select an assignment type (Assign all or Intelligently assign)=
.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can choose between assigning all or one module intelligently.</p><=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-03</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter, sort, and search for available training modules.</p></=
td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter, sort, and search for modules, and modules can be sorte=
d by popularity.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-04</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview the selected training modules before assignment.</p></=
td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can see a preview of the selected training modules.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-05</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must select at least one training module before proceeding.</p></t=
d>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin cannot proceed without selecting at least one training module.</p>=
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-06</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select Days Until Due and Training Scope for the campaign.</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can specify the number of days until due and define training scope=
.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-07</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can toggle advanced options for additional configuration (if avail=
able).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can show or hide advanced options in the modal.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-08</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can specify the training scope, including employees who clicked on=
 payloads or were compromised.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can define the scope of employees who should receive the training.=
</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-09</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can save and continue after selecting and validating the training =
modules.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can click the Save &amp; Continue button and proceed to the next s=
tep.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-10</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can assign all selected modules or intelligently assign one module=
.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can choose the assignment method.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-11</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter training modules based on categories such as security, =
phishing, etc.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply filters to display specific modules based on category.</=
p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-12</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can set a due date for the training and specify the number of days=
 until it=E2=80=99s due.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can specify and view the days until due.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-13</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can configure multiple training modules for different users within=
